WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.228
Imagine spending four hundred dollars on a machine… just to

2
00:00:03.348 --> 00:00:05.701
discover your hands could do the same thing.

3
00:00:07.438 --> 00:00:08.376
Meet Juicero.

4
00:00:08.556 --> 00:00:11.907
A startup that wanted to revolutionize fresh juice.

5
00:00:12.109 --> 00:00:12.762
The idea?

6
00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:17.164
A sophisticated, internet-connected machine that squeezed specially prepared produce

7
00:00:17.284 --> 00:00:17.971
packs.

8
00:00:18.172 --> 00:00:21.403
The pitch was simple: fresh juice, without the mess.

9
00:00:22.877 --> 00:00:26.220
Investors poured approximately one hundred and twenty million dollars into

10
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:26.964
the company.

11
00:00:27.158 --> 00:00:29.715
The machine launched at six hundred and ninety-nine dollars,

12
00:00:29.835 --> 00:00:31.334
before the price was reduced.

13
00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:33.159
It looked like the future of breakfast.

14
00:00:36.141 --> 00:00:39.278
Then Bloomberg tested something nobody wanted to admit.

15
00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.135
The juice packs could be squeezed by hand… and the

16
00:00:42.255 --> 00:00:44.449
machine wasn't necessary for the basic result.

17
00:00:47.539 --> 00:00:50.120
To be fair, Juicero promised consistency,

18
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.331
convenience, and freshness checks.

19
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.440
But the internet only saw the hands.

20
00:00:56.341 --> 00:00:57.785
The backlash was brutal.

21
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.819
Juicero offered refunds and suspended sales in September twenty seventeen.

22
00:01:03.023 --> 00:01:04.160
The company shut down.

23
00:01:07.905 --> 00:01:10.587
And this is where developers should pay attention.

24
00:01:10.789 --> 00:01:13.942
We sometimes spend weeks building complex systems,

25
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:18.191
AI features, and beautiful dashboards… when the customer simply wants

26
00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.326
their problem solved.

27
00:01:20.742 --> 00:01:22.656
So before you build the next big thing,

28
00:01:22.944 --> 00:01:27.175
ask yourself: would the customer still need it without the fancy technology?
